From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:16:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] RISC OS: let the sound thread run when the frame rate is
 behind

SDL_framerateDelay() doesn't wait at all when the game is slower than
its frame limit (always, on a Pi), so the main thread never gave way and
the sound thread mixing OpenAL's output only ran when the thread ticker
preempted it. Call sched_yield() then, as riscos-openttd and VCMI do
after each frame.
---
 lib/framework/SDL_framerate.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/framework/SDL_framerate.c b/lib/framework/SDL_framerate.c
index 0f97ac1..3a04193 100644
--- a/lib/framework/SDL_framerate.c
+++ b/lib/framework/SDL_framerate.c
@@ -8,6 +8,9 @@
  */
 
 #include "SDL_framerate.h"
+#if defined(__riscos__)
+#include <sched.h>
+#endif
 
 /* 
    Initialize the framerate manager
@@ -80,5 +83,10 @@ void SDL_framerateDelay(FPSmanager * manager)
     } else {
 	manager->framecount = 0;
 	manager->lastticks = SDL_GetTicks();
+#if defined(__riscos__)
+	/* Behind the target rate there's no delay, so nothing else ran:
+	 * give SDL's sound thread (OpenAL's mixer) a turn every frame. */
+	sched_yield();
+#endif
     }
 }
